$ ramplus profile apply zswap-lz4 --experimental --yes
Plan: profile zswap-lz4 — experimental: not confirmed by an SSD benchmark
Command: ramplus profile apply zswap-lz4 --experimental
Profile: zswap + lz4. zswap on: lz4, zsmalloc, pool up to 20% of RAM; sysctl as in default.
Evidence: none (no scripts/bench.sh results on a real SSD)

Parameters
  PARAMETER         NOW     NEW       CURRENT SOURCE
  zswap.enabled     N    →  Y         kernel default
  zswap.compressor  lzo  →  lz4       kernel default
  zswap.zpool       —       zsmalloc  not in this kernel — skipped
  unchanged: zswap.max_pool_percent=20, vm.swappiness=60, vm.page-cluster=3, vm.watermark_scale_factor=10, vm.vfs_cache_pressure=100

